                <pb facs="0116" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4035: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-04T08:00:00+02:35">April 4, 1936—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>197. Five Italian planes bombed Addis Ababa at 7:30 this morning. Principal
                    objective was flying field about 4 miles outside city where one Ethiopian plane
                    was completely destroyed. No bombs dropped in town itself nor on wireless
                    station and apparently no casualties anywhere.</p>
                <p>In driving through streets during the raid I saw no signs of panic and the police
                    were at their posts as usual.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
